  "statement": "You're given a string `s` of uppercase English letters and an integer `k`. You may change at most `k` characters of the string, each into any uppercase letter you like.\n\nReturn the length of the longest substring that could consist of one repeated letter after those changes. You only need to report the length, not make the changes.\n\nConstraints: 1 <= len(s) <= 10^5; `s` contains only the letters A-Z; 0 <= k <= len(s).",
